<H3>_________________________________</H3>
<H3>ABBREVIATIONS USED:</H3>
</UL></DL>
<DL>
<UL>
<LI>BIC = Barbie in Chiba store in Japan
<LI>CCC = Cult Couture Collection
<LI>COA = Certificate of Authenticity
<LI>F.PC = Future.Perfect Collection
<LI>FR = Fashion Royalty
<LI>FR-Mono = FR Monogram Collection
<LI>FRMC-R = Moods Collection "Romantic"
<LI>FRVC = Fashion Royalty Voyages Collection
<LI>GC = Glamorous Collection
<LI>GFC = Graphic Flirtation Collection
<LI>HD = Haute Doll magazine
<LI>HRC = Hollywood Royalty Collection
<LI>IFDC = International Fashion Doll Convention
<LI>MAC = Mauve Absolue Collection
<LI>MB = Model Behavior
<LI>MC = Miami Collection
<LI>MFD = My Favourite Doll
<LI>N.FA-N.FC = Nu.Face Agency - Nu.Fantasy Collection
<LI>PC = Premiere Collection
<LI>SdJC = Style du Jour Collection
</UL></DL>
<DL>
<H4>
My thanks to Adrial in Spain who started this list several years ago. I have tweaked it and added 

to it as new dolls/fashions are announced.
<P>A big thanks to Marg at MFD who went out of her way to provide me with extra information about 

the 2005 Jason Wu convention products. And further thanks for looking into the *mystery* purse and 

providing info.
<P>Also a big thank you to Alain Tremblay who provided me with information about the 2007 Royal 

Life, AND the 2008 The Heist, event exclusives! It is much appreciated!!
<P>And many thanks to Mary of Mary T's Doll House! I am so grateful for all her help in obtaining 

stock #'s and other general info as needed.
<P>I do not collect Misaki and find I cannot keep up with her releases, therefore the FR: Nippon 

section has been removed from the list.
<P>~*~ Re: Saks Agnes - A W Club Yahoo group (now defunct) post #13300 dated 12/23/06 stated, 

"There were a handful of dolls (no name, no story, no anything) put together by Jason to be given 

to Saks Fifth Avenue Buyers at a luncheon honoring Jason for his people-sized collection. They are 

not part of the Fashion Royalty line. This was a promotional fashion industry thank you item that 

is unaffiliated with Integrity or the doll lines in general." 
<br>Given the rarity of this doll on ebay and the above statement, I personally believe that ebay 

auctions stating that the edition size of this doll is 100 pieces is an *ebay myth* perpetuated 

from seller to seller but with no basis in fact. Therefore, the edition size for my list will 

remain "??" until I hear differently from a reliable source.
</H4>
 

